# Workbooks Excel saved for the cell writer's tests: formats, shared and array
# formulas, a calc chain, spills with their metadata, a table, 1904 dates.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/CellWriterFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/CellStylesFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/FormulaTableFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/DynamicArrayFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/Date1904Fixture.xlsm
# Workbooks Excel saved for the shape tools' tests: AutoShapes, a text box, a
# line, a group, form controls, a picture and a chart, macros assigned.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesPictureChartFixture.xlsm
# A workbook holding one of every form control Excel offers, each with a
# linked cell, for the tests that pin what a shape edit must leave alone.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ControlsFixture.xlsm
# The shape fixtures after each application set a fill, an outline, a font,
# a rotation, hidden and a new stacking order on them and saved: the markup
# the shape formatting reader and writer are held to.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesFormattedFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesFormattedFixture.pptm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesFormattedFixture.docm
# WordShapesFixture after Word turned AnchoredBox 90 degrees, brought it to
# the front, hid one shape in the canvas and restyled the other.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/ShapesArrangedFixture.docm
# One file per container shape, saved by the live application in a
# macro-capable format and never given any VBA: what a workbook saved as
# .xlsm before the first macro looks like on disk. Ground truth for telling
# "this file holds no code" apart from "this file could not be read".
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaFixture.docm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaFixture.xls
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaFixture.ppt
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaFixture.pptm
# Saved by Excel with no VBA: a chart sheet in front of three worksheets,
# renamed and reordered (NoVbaSheetsFixture), and a worksheet beside a
# dialog sheet and an Excel 4 macro sheet (NoVbaOtherSheetsFixture). What
# "Add VBA Project" is measured against: Excel names and makes modules for
# these exactly as the add-VBA tests expect.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaSheetsFixture.xlsm
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaOtherSheetsFixture.xlsm
# The first workbook saved as .xlsb, and Excel's own copy of it once VBA was
# added: the records XLIDE writes into a binary workbook are compared with
# Excel's, byte for byte.
!tests/fixtures/binaries/NoVbaSheetsFixture.xlsb
!tests/fixtures/binaries/VbaAddedByExcelFixture.xlsb
